{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "06L0", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-presentation-deformation-categories}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6ec77d46a1a3966a80510f92aa7bb84c18719a7d2502792c2ed6717cba1117de", "source_text": "Presentations of deformation categories", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4e4b35ca7266f8a32477ad9cbda1f2db270d1275220a7322ff87c0697d065a58", "unit_id": "tag:06L0:title"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06L0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2dcb778ede4329b6e71133d05e099b677ddfe9365950cb12abe1674abb2ad6ed", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:75fcdc0cea9bb4a9e2ed6e49f3df3052b59b2706ed03525efb9a52d6ec57ba9c", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nAccording to the next lemma, a smooth morphism from a predeformation functor to\na predeformation category <MATH_0001> gives rise to a presentation of\n<MATH_0002> by a smooth groupoid in functors.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:156fddf13d3de5d9d9a1295d5d19cadb20a237eeb71e8bd37aaec4a68d4a2ca8", "unit_id": "tag:06L0:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06L0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0003": "$U : \\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0004": "$f : U \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0007": "$f : U \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0008": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0009": "$f : U(k) \\to \\mathcal{F}(k)$", "MATH_0010": "$[f] : [U/R] \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-presentation-construction}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-presentation-morphism}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-smooth-groupoid-in-functors-construction}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9c1bac96719bd88222126945b0c78f00597d47ac7cf517a183a1090a8aa8874e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b7ac4f66c484410f6a435db662b72de025211ec1b1b27f251b2dd4bc52d58d64", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a category cofibered in groupoids over\n<MATH_0002>. Let <MATH_0003>\nbe a functor. Let <MATH_0004> be a smooth morphism of\ncategories cofibered in groupoids. Then:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> If <MATH_0005> is the groupoid in functors on\n<MATH_0006> constructed from <MATH_0007> in\nLemma <REF_0001>, then <MATH_0008>\nis smooth.\n<STRUCT_0003> If <MATH_0009> is essentially surjective,\nthen the morphism <MATH_0010> of\nLemma <REF_0002>\nis an equivalence.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6edef68d3ae5c4d84e078fa21880686e670e9bfac35a3cc170a269bce012153b", "unit_id": "tag:06L1:statement"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06L0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nR = U \\times_{f, \\mathcal{F}, f} U \\ar[r]_-s \\ar[d]_t & U\n\\ar[d]^f \\\\\nU \\ar[r]^f & \\mathcal{F}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$t, s$", "MATH_0003": "$t, s$", "MATH_0004": "$f : U \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$[f] : [U/R] \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-presentation-construction}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-smooth-properties}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-smooth-morphism-essentially-surjective}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-presentation-morphism}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2a3396c914cba0753417597517b12fa085f4e2335314185ce8a7642347fc5742", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c0016c3f0cd029724fd4829a554838ff370d4f5c307cf4da9f3251bf0ae4fa0d", "source_text": "From the construction of\nLemma <REF_0001>\nwe have a commutative diagram\n<MATH_0001>\nwhere <MATH_0002> are the first and second projections.  So <MATH_0003> are smooth by\nLemma <REF_0002>.  Hence (1) holds.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nIf the assumption of (2) holds, then by\nLemma <REF_0003>\nthe morphism <MATH_0004> is essentially surjective. Hence by\nLemma <REF_0004>\nthe morphism <MATH_0005> is an equivalence.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8fbcadad77188652beb632b2e069fa2bb29be6a35e37a6a19e9a324a52e2ecfe", "unit_id": "tag:06L1:proof"}
